{"hits":{"hits":[{"updated":"2025-10-31T21:20:58.668140+00:00","created":"2021-03-22T00:00:00+00:00","metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"127","pubinfo_freetext":"Phys. Rev. Lett. 127, 131603 (2021)","artid":"131603","material":"publication","year":2021,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"},"journal_issue":"13","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."}],"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"source":"APS","value":"Kavli Institute for Cosmological Physics and Enrico Fermi Institute, University of Chicago, Chicago, Illinois 60637, USA"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"kolb, edward w.","full_name":"Kolb, Edward W.","curated_relation":true,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1002355"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"E.W.Kolb.1"}],"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902730"},"value":"Chicago U., EFI"},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/908957"},"value":"Chicago U., KICP"}],"last_name":"Kolb","signature_block":"CALBe","first_name":"Edward W.","uuid":"2d6a209b-048c-4a76-9ab7-374eb8265165","recid":1002355},{"raw_affiliations":[{"source":"APS","value":"Department of Physics and Astronomy, Rice University, Houston, Texas 77005, USA"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"long, andrew j.","full_name":"Long, Andrew J.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1069459"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Andrew.J.Long.1"}],"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903156"},"value":"Rice U."}],"last_name":"Long","signature_block":"LANGa","first_name":"Andrew J.","uuid":"dc75135f-4044-444b-bb84-505cf841b2e1","recid":1069459},{"raw_affiliations":[{"source":"APS","value":"Kavli Institute for Cosmological Physics and Enrico Fermi Institute, University of Chicago, Chicago, Illinois 60637, USA"},{"source":"APS","value":"Department of Physics, University of Winnipeg, Winnipeg, MB R3B 2E9, Canada"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"mcdonough, evan","full_name":"McDonough, Evan","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1272159"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Evan.McDonough.1"}],"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902730"},"value":"Chicago U., EFI"},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/908957"},"value":"Chicago U., KICP"}],"last_name":"McDonough","signature_block":"MCDANAGHe","first_name":"Evan","uuid":"6f7516b8-3075-4d19-9bf2-f563708ddafc","recid":1272159}],"imprints":[{"date":"2021-09-24"}],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"We extend the swampland from effective field theories (EFTs) inconsistent with quantum gravity to EFTs inconsistent with quantum supergravity. This enlarges the swampland to include EFTs that become inconsistent when the gravitino is quantized. We propose the “gravitino swampland conjecture”: the gravitino sound speed must be nonvanishing in all EFTs that are low-energy limits of quantum supergravity. This seemingly simple statement has important consequences for both theories and observations. The conjecture is consistent with and supported by the Kachru-Kallosh-Linde-Trivedi and large volume scenarios for moduli stabilization in string theory.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We extend the swampland from effective field theories (EFTs) inconsistent with quantum gravity to EFTs inconsistent with quantum supergravity. This enlarges the swampland to include EFTs that become inconsistent when the gravitino is quantized. We propose the Gravitino Swampland Conjecture: the gravitino sound speed must be non-vanishing in all EFTs that are low energy limits of quantum supergravity. This seemingly simple statement has important consequences for both theories and observations. The conjecture is consistent with and supported by the KKLT and LVS scenarios for moduli stabilization in string theory.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_